Subject: Build signond and libsignon-qt against Qt 6

The 8.61 release names its client library, pkg-config file and CMake package
`qt5` whatever Qt builds it. This takes the names from QT_MAJOR_VERSION
(libsignon-qt6, SignOnQt6), moves the plugin data stream and the D-Bus output
parameters to Qt 6 types, and ports the uses of API Qt 6 removed. It is the
difference from the VERSION_8.61 tag to the head of upstream merge request
!36 ("Add Qt6 support", commit c8ad9824), which Alpine's signond builds from,
including the one commit between the tag and the request's base, which drops
the superuser check from `make install`.

